From ed6b714d02210dc3af28920a8fe9c2444ab2b73e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:34:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Show a stereoscopic 3D video to both eyes, with a 3D menu

A stereoscopic 3D video holds both views in every frame, in one of the
packings of the frame packing arrangement SEI (H.264 Table D-8, H.265
Table D.8) or of Matroska's StereoMode (RFC 9559), and was shown as it is
stored: both views squeezed or mixed into one picture. Qt Multimedia now tells
the packing of the frames (QVideoFrameFormat::stereoMode), and a new
StereoFilter between the media player and the video output takes the two
views out of every packing there is: side by side and top and bottom, side by
side with quincunx sampling, row and column interleaved, checkerboard and frame
sequential. Anaglyph videos hold both views mixed and are shown as they are.

Under a compositor that takes stereo content declarations
(kde_stereo_content_v1, with wl_subcompositor, wp_viewporter and wl_shm), a 3D
video is drawn into a surface of its own under the window's surface: both views
side by side at the size of one view, the left eye first, and declared as full
side by side. The on-screen display and the menus stay in the window's surface
over it, a 2D surface the same in both eyes. Elsewhere the left view is shown.

The video is a StereoVideo, which is a Video with the filter and the layer in
it. The on-screen display gets a 3D button that opens a menu in the style of the
file menu, for a remote control: the view (3D, left, right, both), the input
format for a video that does not say it is 3D or says it wrong (every packing,
half and full size views of side by side and top and bottom told apart, or not
3D) and Swap Eyes. The choice is for the file it was made for. A video that says
nothing, and is at least 2.5 times as wide as high, is taken as full size views
side by side.

The parts are used where they are found at configure time: Qt Multimedia with
QVideoFrameFormat::StereoMode, and for the layer wayland-client, QtGuiPrivate
and libstereo-declare. Without them Plank Player plays as before.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
